The rest of Gehenom went pretty much the same way.  I lost one of
Movanic Devas on Orcus' level, (purple worm) and had another slowed.  I
never found a way to speed it back up, since wands of speed monster
didn't seem to work, and I couldn't get it to pick something up.  I
guess I could have tried hitting it with a potion of speed, but I
didn't think of the idea at the time.

For Dispater's level (the one with the long winding passage), I dug
down at every fire trap disabling them.  The pits generated didn't
bother me since I was wearing the amulet of flying.

At some point here I had enchanted my weapons up, lost some enchantment
to a steel golem (Maybe in Frankenstein's lab), then enchanted them up
again.  I also got my ring of increase damage to +5, and finally got my
strength to 18/**.  Altogether, I was doing around 80 points of damage
a turn.  I got lucky and managed to take out both Greygon and Dispater
without them having a chance to run away (two turns at once).  With
this setup I became an unstoppable killing machine, and even discarded
the fiction of carrying daggers around "just in case".  I didn't even
bother playing with guns...  (Though I still carried around a wand of
death "just in case").

At some point here I found something called "Doomblade", a chaotic
sword.  From the name it sounded like something worth having for the
Astral plane (since Mojo is not as useful there), but I decided not to
bother since it kept zapping me.  I did stash it and take it with me on
my ascension run though.

Found the vibrating square, went to Vlad's tower, and found that I
couldn't get in.  Went all the way back to level 12 to fetch the other
keys.  On the way I decided to replace my missing pets.  Got a Planetar
(with Demonbane) quite easily, and the Wallet of Perseus - which seems
like a real handy artifact to have around.

Cleared out Vlad's tower, got the candelabrum, and cleared out the zoo
at the bottom of the wizards tower.  Went back to my stashes to get
ready for the ascension run.  Did some alchemy and got my hitpoints to
~500.  Used some magic markers I found to get my AC down.  Switched my
dwarven mithril to GDSM (so I could wear an oilskin cloak on water
without losing MR).  Decided I wanted to see what the most powerful
kind of pet Tyr might let me have so I drank some !oGL to get to level
30 (I was gaining levels only by killing monsters and got to level 25,
a big change from Vanilla.  Sure the monster are harder and give more
XP, but it's also probably easier to gain levels in Slashem).  A couple
of sacrifices later Tyr gave me a Solar.  Pretty  cool!!  Those guys
can get to level 49 without problems, can't be hit by anything normal,
and are pretty tough.  Still won't pick up weapons though.  Getting one
through a figurine and "pumping" it would really be scary!

I tried getting TC from tengu tins, but only got "jumpy".  Instead I
bought a ring of TC from the black market.  Left with 300,000 zorkmids
in credit.  Next time.


So me and the Planetar and the Solar walked down through hell.  I dug
out some wall to help my final run.  Woke the Wizard, and killed him
(/oD I think).  Teleported to the bottom.  Preformed the ritual, except
that I forgot to light the candelabrum, and ended up summoning some
undead...  Re-did the invocation and teleported into the sanctum for
the shortcut.  I didn't exactly work, since I neglected to plan for any
fast getaway and ended up going though the graveyard on the way out
with no real way of retreat (OK, I could have dropped the amulet and
used the orb, but still).

I didn't have a wand of secret door detection, so that was a hassle,
and with a lack of reflection I hesitated hitting the high priest of
Moloch.  Fortunately, my Solar was more than up for the job.  Getting
out was not easy.  There were tons of summoning monsters (and at least
one summoning from the amulet), but nothing touched my pets.  Finally
(as usual), something summoned a cockatrice, and even though I was
flying, I made sure not to move while wielding it - didn't really need
to.  The monsters all came to me.

Since I already had the amulet, I didn't bother with the chests in the
graveyard, but instead ran for the exit.  The lack of mysterious force
was great, but I kept on worrying that I wasn't carrying the amulet
anymore.  the wizard tried to stop me a few times, but he didn't prove
too much trouble.  80 hitpoint a turn + Very fast+ pet Solar = Lots of
damage.

I was worried that the planes might have been "enhanced" in some
Slash'em way, but everything seemed normal.  Air elementals were no
problem with half damage - and because I hit hard enough to take them
down in two rounds.  I made sure not to go through the clouds because
of the lack of reflection.  There were two "Vorpal Jabberwocks" that I
stayed clear of, not being sure what the "vorpal" stood for in this
case. The Solar got them.  Put on an oilskin for water, and made sure
my pets went though the portal before me.  On Astral I found Famine on
the right, Pest in the middle and Death on the left.  Went left, and
wiped the floor with everything I found.  Death fell in one turn the
first time.  My Solar (and Planetar) took care of him the other times.
Angels are shock resistant, so Mojo wasn't as useful, but I was still
doing enough damage.  The first altar was the correct one, but I had
gone through without using any of my unrenewable resources, so I
decided to clear the entire astral plane and went to visit the other
altars.  Nothing interesting, though I did pick up an artifact mace
(Disrupter?)  and a silver mace.

I cleared everything out, than went back to the lawful altar, checked
my inventory, drank my potions of healing, summoned my pets and:



